; Test: == operator (expression constructor/unifier)
; ==================================================
;
; == doesn't "check equality" - it CONSTRUCTS expressions!
; Pattern: (== <expr> $var) builds <expr> and binds $var to it

(LHS (foo $y))
(RHS ($x bar))

; How this works:
; 1. (BTM (LHS $x)) queries space, finds (LHS (foo $y))
;    Binds: $x = (foo $y)
; 2. (== (RHS $x) $o) constructs (RHS (foo $y))
;    Binds: $o = (RHS (foo $y))  [note: variables get fresh names like $a]
; 3. Output: (+ (REM $o)) produces (REM (RHS ($a bar)))

(exec 0
  (I (BTM (LHS $x))
     (== (RHS $x) $o))
  (O (+ (REM $o))
     (- $o)))

; Expected: (REM (RHS ($a bar)))
;
; Key insight: == is an expression CONSTRUCTOR, not a comparison!
; It builds new expressions from patterns with variable substitution.
